-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_55.sql (Isaiah 55) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 55 — THE GOSPEL-INVITATION chapter that closes the Servant-songs arc. *Ho, every
-- one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters... buy wine and milk without money and without price*
-- (55:1) — the free invitation to the living water (John 7:37 *If any man thirst, let him come unto
-- me, and drink*; John 4:14; Revelation 21:6 / 22:17 *whosoever will, let him take the water of life
-- freely*). But it is NOT cheap grace: the invitation is to *Incline your ear, and come unto me:
-- hear, and your soul shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure
-- mercies of David* (55:3) — covenant-obedience, the Davidic covenant fulfilled in Messiah (Paul
-- quotes 55:3 in Acts 13:34, the resurrection securing the *sure mercies of David*). The Davidic
-- witness/leader is given and the nations called (55:4-5 -> Romans 15:12 the root of Jesse; Revelation
-- 1:5 the faithful witness). The call to repentance is teshuvah, not antinomian: *Seek ye Yahuah while
-- he may be found... Let the wicked forsake his way... and let him return unto Yahuah, and he will
-- have mercy upon him* (55:6-7 -> 2 Corinthians 6:2 the accepted time; Acts 17:27 sought that they
-- might find). The transcendence of Yahuah's ways (55:8-9 -> Romans 11:33). And the chapter's heart:
-- ★★★ *So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void* (55:11)
-- — THE efficacious Word, the spoken Word that goes forth and accomplishes = the Formed Son (John
-- 1:1-3,14 the Word made flesh; Hebrews 4:12 the word quick and powerful; 1 Peter 1:23-25 the word
-- that liveth and abideth; Mark 4:14 the sower sows the word). It closes with the second-Exodus joyful
-- return and creation restored: *ye shall go out with joy... instead of the thorn shall come up the
-- fir tree... and it shall be to Yahuah for a name, an everlasting sign* (55:12-13 -> Isaiah 35:10 the
-- ransomed return with songs; Genesis 3:18 the thorn-curse reversed; Romans 8:19-21 the creation
-- released).
