--   7. isaiah-55-ye-shall-go-out-with-joy-instead-of-the-thorn — NT (Romans 8) + Tanakh (Isaiah 35, Genesis 3) [free]
--      (★★ the second-Exodus joyful return + creation restored; the thorn-curse of Eden reversed; an everlasting sign)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★★★ HO, EVERY ONE THAT THIRSTETH (THREAD 1): *Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters,
--      and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and
--      without price* (55:1). The free invitation to the living water — Yahusha cries it on the last
--      great day of the feast: *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink* (John 7:37); *the
--      water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life*
--      (John 4:14). And the Spirit and the bride echo it at the canon's end: *I will give unto him that
--      is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely* (Revelation 21:6); *whosoever will, let
--      him take the water of life freely* (Revelation 22:17). Wisdom's own invitation in Sirach is the
--      near-parallel: *Come to me, all you that be desirous of me, and fill yourselves with my fruits...
--      They that eat me shall yet be hungry, and they that drink me shall yet be thirsty* (Sirach
--      24:19,21) — the same come-and-be-filled call, the thirst that only Wisdom/the Word satisfies.
--   ★★ THE SURE MERCIES OF DAVID (THREAD 2): *Incline your ear, and come unto me: hear, and your soul
--      shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David*
--      (55:3). NOT cheap grace — the invitation is to *hear* and *incline the ear* (covenant-obedience),
--      the everlasting covenant. The *sure mercies of David* are the Davidic covenant fulfilled in
--      Messiah: Paul quotes this verse of the resurrection — *as concerning that he raised him up from
--      the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he said on this wise, I will give you the sure
--      mercies of David* (Acts 13:34). The resurrection of the Son of David secures the everlasting
--      covenant; the sure mercies are made sure in the risen One.
--   ★ A WITNESS, A LEADER, THE NATIONS (THREAD 3): *Behold, I have given him for a witness to the people,
--      a leader and commander to the people. Behold, thou shalt call a nation that thou knowest not, and
--      nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee* (55:4-5). The Davidic witness/leader is the root
--      of Jesse in whom the nations trust: *There shall be a root of Jesse, and he that shall rise to
--      reign over the Gentiles; in him shall the Gentiles trust* (Romans 15:12). And the witness is named
--      at the canon's opening: *Yahusha (Jesus)... who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of
--      the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth* (Revelation 1:5) — leader and commander, the
--      two-house and nations ingathering running unto him.
--   ★★ SEEK YE YAHUAH (THREAD 4): *Seek ye Yahuah (LORD) while he may be found, call ye upon him while he
--      is near: Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return
--      unto Yahuah (LORD), and he will have mercy upon him; and to our Elohim (God), for he will
--      abundantly pardon* (55:6-7). This is teshuvah — forsake-the-way-and-return — NOT antinomian:
--      the pardon is abundant for the one who TURNS. Paul presses the urgency: *behold, now is the
--      accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation* (2 Corinthians 6:2). And the seeking finds:
--      *That they should seek Yahuah (Lord), if haply they might feel after him, and find him, though he
--      be not far from every one of us* (Acts 17:27) — sought while near, found, the wicked who forsakes
--      his way abundantly pardoned.
--   ★★ MY WAYS ARE HIGHER (THREAD 5): *For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my
--      ways, saith Yahuah (LORD). For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher
--      than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts* (55:8-9). The transcendence of the Father's
--      ways above man's. Paul breaks into the same doxology: *O the depth of the riches both of the
--      wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past
--      finding out!* (Romans 11:33); *For who hath known the mind of the Lord?* (Romans 11:34). The
--      mercy that pardons the wicked (v.7) is grounded in the higher ways — man cannot search them out.
--   ★★★ MY WORD SHALL NOT RETURN VOID (THREAD 6): *For as the rain cometh down, and the snow from heaven,
--      and returneth not thither, but watereth the earth... So shall my word be that goeth forth out of
--      my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please*
--      (55:10-11). THE efficacious Word — the spoken Word that goes forth and accomplishes is the Formed
--      Son, the Word drawn from the Formless: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with
--      Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)... All things were made by him* (John 1:1,3); *And the
--      Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us* (John 1:14). The living and powerful Word: *the word of
--      Elohim (God) is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword* (Hebrews 4:12). The word
--      that abides: *Being born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, by the word of
--      Elohim (God), which liveth and abideth for ever* (1 Peter 1:23); *the word of Yahuah (Lord)
--      endureth for ever* (1 Peter 1:25). And the seed-and-harvest figure of v.10 (*that it may give seed
--      to the sower*) is the sower's parable: *The sower soweth the word* (Mark 4:14). The Word sent
--      forth always accomplishes; it never returns void.
--   ★★ YE SHALL GO OUT WITH JOY (THREAD 7): *For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace:
--      the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing... Instead of the thorn
--      shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree: and it shall
--      be to Yahuah (LORD) for a name, for an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off* (55:12-13). The
--      second-Exodus joyful return — *the ransomed of Yahuah (LORD) shall return, and come to Zion with
--      songs and everlasting joy upon their heads* (Isaiah 35:10). And the thorn that comes up the fir
--      tree is the reversal of Eden's curse: *Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee*
--      (Genesis 3:18) — the cursed ground healed, creation restored. Paul names the groaning released:
--      *the earnest expectation of the creature waiteth for the manifestation of the sons of Elohim
--      (God)* (Romans 8:19); *the creature itself also shall be delivered from the bondage of corruption
--      into the glorious liberty of the children of Elohim (God)* (Romans 8:21). The redeemed go out with
--      joy; the thorn-curse is reversed; an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off.
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.2 (the spending money for that which is not bread — the contrast that
--      opens the invitation of v.1, bound into THREAD 1), v.5b (because of Yahuah... for he hath glorified
--      thee — the close of the witness/nations block, woven into THREAD 3), v.12b-13a (the trees clap
--      their hands / the brier and myrtle — the body of the restoration figure, bound into THREAD 7). All
--      recorded, none silently skipped. Extras: weighed Sirach 24 (Wisdom's invitation — ADDED to THREAD 1)
--      and Wisdom of Solomon; no further clean single-verse extras witness warranted — held in prose.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa55_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★★★): Ho, every one that thirsteth — the free invitation to the living water
    ('canon','isaiah',55,1,'canon','john',7,37,'free',
      E'*In the last day, that great day of the feast, Yahusha (Jesus) stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink* (John 7:37). *Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters... come, buy wine and milk without money and without price* (Isaiah 55:1) is the very cry Yahusha lifts on the last day of the feast — the free invitation to the living water, the thirsty called to come and drink without price.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,1,'canon','john',4,14,'free',
      E'*But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life* (John 4:14). The waters to which *every one that thirsteth* is called (Isaiah 55:1) are the well springing up into everlasting life that Yahusha gives — the thirst answered once for all, the free gift without money or price.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,1,'canon','revelation',21,6,'free',
      E'*It is done. I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end. I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely* (Revelation 21:6). *Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters... without money and without price* (Isaiah 55:1) is fulfilled at the consummation — *the fountain of the water of life freely* to him that is athirst; the invitation of the prophet is the gift of the end.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,1,'canon','revelation',22,17,'free',
      E'*And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely* (Revelation 22:17). *Come ye to the waters... buy wine and milk without money and without price* (Isaiah 55:1) is the canon''s closing call — *whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely*; the thirsty bidden come, the water without price.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,1,'apocrypha','ecclesiasticus',24,19,'extras',
      E'*Come to me, all you that be desirous of me, and fill yourselves with my fruits* (Sirach 24:19). Wisdom''s invitation parallels the prophet''s: *Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters... come ye, buy, and eat* (Isaiah 55:1) — the same come-and-be-filled call, all the desirous bidden to come and eat freely of what satisfies.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,2,'apocrypha','ecclesiasticus',24,21,'extras',
      E'*They that eat me shall yet be hungry, and they that drink me shall yet be thirsty* (Sirach 24:21). *Wherefore do ye spend money for that which is not bread? and your labour for that which satisfieth not? hearken diligently unto me, and eat ye that which is good* (Isaiah 55:2) — Wisdom answers the same hunger: only she, the Word, satisfies; the bread that is not bread leaves the soul empty, but the desirous keep coming to be filled.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★★): The everlasting covenant, the sure mercies of David (NOT cheap grace)
    ('canon','isaiah',55,3,'canon','acts',13,34,'free',
      E'*And as concerning that he raised him up from the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he said on this wise, I will give you the sure mercies of David* (Acts 13:34). Paul quotes Isaiah 55:3 — *I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David* — of the resurrection. The Son of David raised, no more to see corruption, secures the everlasting covenant; the sure mercies are made sure in the risen One.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★): A witness, a leader, the nations shall run unto thee
    ('canon','isaiah',55,4,'canon','revelation',1,5,'free',
      E'*And from Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ), who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth* (Revelation 1:5). *Behold, I have given him for a witness to the people, a leader and commander to the people* (Isaiah 55:4) — the Davidic witness/leader is Yahusha the faithful witness, the prince of the kings of the earth; the leader and commander given to the people.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,5,'canon','romans',15,12,'free',
      E'*And again, Esaias saith, There shall be a root of Jesse, and he that shall rise to reign over the Gentiles; in him shall the Gentiles trust* (Romans 15:12). *Behold, thou shalt call a nation that thou knowest not, and nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee* (Isaiah 55:5) — the nations called are the Gentiles who trust in the root of Jesse, running unto him because of Yahuah; the two-house and nations ingathering to the Davidic leader.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★★): Seek ye Yahuah while he may be found — teshuvah, the abundant pardon
    ('canon','isaiah',55,6,'canon','2-corinthians',6,2,'free',
      E'*For he saith, I have heard thee in a time accepted, and in the day of salvation have I succoured thee: behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation* (2 Corinthians 6:2). *Seek ye Yahuah (LORD) while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near* (Isaiah 55:6) — the window is now; Paul presses the same urgency: the accepted time, the day of salvation, the One found while near.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,7,'canon','acts',17,27,'free',
      E'*That they should seek Yahuah (Lord), if haply they might feel after him, and find him, though he be not far from every one of us* (Acts 17:27). *Let the wicked forsake his way... and let him return unto Yahuah (LORD), and he will have mercy upon him... for he will abundantly pardon* (Isaiah 55:7) — the seeking finds, for he is not far; the wicked who forsakes his way and returns (teshuvah) is abundantly pardoned, not the antinomian who keeps his way.'),

    -- THREAD 5 (★★): My ways are higher than your ways
    ('canon','isaiah',55,9,'canon','romans',11,33,'free',
      E'*O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* (Romans 11:33). *For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts* (Isaiah 55:9) — Paul breaks into the same wonder: the ways past finding out, the higher ways man cannot search; the mercy that pardons the wicked (55:7) grounded in the transcendence above man''s thoughts.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,8,'canon','romans',11,34,'free',
      E'*For who hath known the mind of the Lord? or who hath been his counsellor?* (Romans 11:34). *For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith Yahuah (LORD)* (Isaiah 55:8) — none has known the mind of Yahuah; his thoughts are not man''s thoughts, his ways above man''s ways, unsearchable and not to be counselled.'),

    -- THREAD 6 (★★★): My word shall not return unto me void — the efficacious Word, the Formed Son
    ('canon','isaiah',55,11,'canon','john',1,1,'free',
      E'*In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)* (John 1:1). *So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please* (Isaiah 55:11) — the Word that goes forth and accomplishes is the Word that was in the beginning, with Elohim and Elohim, the expressed Word drawn from the Formless by whom all things were made.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,11,'canon','john',1,14,'free',
      E'*And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth* (John 1:14). *My word... that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void* (Isaiah 55:11) goes forth and is made flesh — the Formed Son, the spoken Word who dwelt among us and accomplished all that the Father pleased.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,11,'canon','hebrews',4,12,'free',
      E'*For the word of Elohim (God) is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit* (Hebrews 4:12). *So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth... it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it* (Isaiah 55:11) — the word sent forth is living and powerful; it pierces, it accomplishes, it prospers; it never returns void.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,11,'canon','1-peter',1,23,'free',
      E'*Being born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, by the word of Elohim (God), which liveth and abideth for ever* (1 Peter 1:23). *My word... shall not return unto me void* (Isaiah 55:11) is the word that *liveth and abideth for ever* — the incorruptible seed (echoing the seed of v.10 given to the sower) by which the people are born again; the Word that does not fail.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,11,'canon','1-peter',1,25,'free',
      E'*But the word of Yahuah (Lord) endureth for ever. And this is the word which by the gospel is preached unto you* (1 Peter 1:25). *So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void* (Isaiah 55:11) — the word of Yahuah that *endureth for ever*, the abiding Word preached as the gospel; sent forth, it always accomplishes.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,10,'canon','mark',4,14,'free',
      E'*The sower soweth the word* (Mark 4:14). *For as the rain cometh down... that it may give seed to the sower, and bread to the eater* (Isaiah 55:10) — the seed-and-harvest figure is the sower''s parable: the word is the seed sown, watered by the rain from heaven, bringing forth fruit; the Word that goes forth (55:11) never sown in vain.'),

    -- THREAD 7 (★★): Ye shall go out with joy — the second Exodus, the thorn-curse reversed
    ('canon','isaiah',55,12,'canon','isaiah',35,10,'free',
      E'*And the ransomed of Yahuah (LORD) shall return, and come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads: they shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away* (Isaiah 35:10). *For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace* (Isaiah 55:12) — the second-Exodus return; the ransomed come to Zion with songs, joy and gladness, the joyful regathering of the redeemed.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,13,'canon','genesis',3,18,'free',
      E'*Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee; and thou shalt eat the herb of the field* (Genesis 3:18). *Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree* (Isaiah 55:13) — the curse on the ground in Eden, the thorn and thistle, is reversed; the cursed soil healed, the fir and myrtle in place of thorn and brier, *an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,12,'canon','romans',8,19,'free',
      E'*For the earnest expectation of the creature waiteth for the manifestation of the sons of Elohim (God)* (Romans 8:19). *The mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing, and all the trees of the field shall clap their hands* (Isaiah 55:12) — creation itself rejoices at the redeemed going out; the earnest expectation of the creature, the whole field clapping its hands at the manifestation of the sons of Elohim.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',55,13,'canon','romans',8,21,'free',
      E'*Because the creature itself also shall be delivered from the bondage of corruption into the glorious liberty of the children of Elohim (God)* (Romans 8:21). *Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree... and it shall be to Yahuah (LORD) for a name, for an everlasting sign* (Isaiah 55:13) — the thorn-cursed creation delivered from corruption into glorious liberty; the everlasting sign that shall not be cut off, creation restored with the children of Elohim.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa55_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa55_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-ho-every-one-that-thirsteth-come-ye-to-the-waters',
       E'Ho, every one that thirsteth — come ye to the waters, without money and without price',
       E'The gospel-invitation chapter opens with a free, urgent call to the thirsty: *Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price. Wherefore do ye spend money for that which is not bread? and your labour for that which satisfieth not? hearken diligently unto me, and eat ye that which is good* (Isaiah 55:1-2). Yahusha lifts this very cry on the last great day of the feast: *If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink* (John 7:37); *the water that I shall give him shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life* (John 4:14). And the canon closes with the same free invitation: *I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely* (Revelation 21:6); *the Spirit and the bride say, Come... And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely* (Revelation 22:17). Wisdom''s own invitation is the near-parallel: *Come to me, all you that be desirous of me, and fill yourselves with my fruits... They that eat me shall yet be hungry, and they that drink me shall yet be thirsty* (Sirach 24:19,21) — the same come-and-be-filled call, the bread-that-is-not-bread that leaves the soul empty answered by the Word that alone satisfies. The waters are free, without money and without price; but the call is to *hearken diligently* and *eat that which is good* — to come and drink of the living water, the Word himself.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 27350
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=2
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-the-everlasting-covenant-the-sure-mercies-of-david',
       E'The everlasting covenant — even the sure mercies of David, secured in the resurrection',
       E'The invitation to the waters is not cheap grace; it is a call to covenant: *Incline your ear, and come unto me: hear, and your soul shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David* (Isaiah 55:3). To *incline the ear* and *hear* is covenant-obedience — the soul lives by hearkening. And the *sure mercies of David* are the Davidic covenant fulfilled in Messiah, the Son of David raised: Paul quotes this very verse of the resurrection — *And as concerning that he raised him up from the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he said on this wise, I will give you the sure mercies of David* (Acts 13:34). The everlasting covenant is sealed not by the death of David but by the resurrection of David''s greater Son, who *no more returns to corruption*; the mercies are made sure in the risen One. The thirsty who come and hear enter the everlasting covenant, the unbreakable Davidic promise fulfilled.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27353
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=3
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=3
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-a-witness-a-leader-the-nations-shall-run-unto-thee',
       E'A witness, a leader and commander — the nations shall run unto thee',
       E'The everlasting covenant of David has a witness and a head: *Behold, I have given him for a witness to the people, a leader and commander to the people. Behold, thou shalt call a nation that thou knowest not, and nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee because of Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God), and for the Holy One of Yashar''el (Israel); for he hath glorified thee* (Isaiah 55:4-5). The Davidic witness/leader is Yahusha named at the canon''s opening: *Yahusha HaMashiach (Jesus Christ), who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth* (Revelation 1:5) — leader and commander, the prince of the kings. And the nations called are the Gentiles who trust in the root of Jesse: *There shall be a root of Jesse, and he that shall rise to reign over the Gentiles; in him shall the Gentiles trust* (Romans 15:12). The nations that *knew not thee* run unto the glorified Davidic Witness — the two-house and the nations ingathering to the leader given for the people, because of Yahuah and the Holy One of Yashar''el.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27356
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=4
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=5
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-seek-ye-yahuah-while-he-may-be-found',
       E'Seek ye Yahuah while he may be found — forsake the way and return, the abundant pardon',
       E'The invitation turns to a call to repentance with a now-or-never urgency: *Seek ye Yahuah (LORD) while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near: Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return unto Yahuah (LORD), and he will have mercy upon him; and to our Elohim (God), for he will abundantly pardon* (Isaiah 55:6-7). This is teshuvah — forsake-the-way-and-return — never antinomian: the abundant pardon is for the one who TURNS, who forsakes the wicked way. Paul presses the same urgency of the accepted moment: *behold, now is the accepted time; behold, now is the day of salvation* (2 Corinthians 6:2). And the seeking finds, for he is near: *That they should seek Yahuah (Lord), if haply they might feel after him, and find him, though he be not far from every one of us* (Acts 17:27). Yahuah may be found while he is near; the wicked who forsakes his way and returns is met with mercy and abundantly pardoned — but the pardon comes through the turning, not apart from it.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27359
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=6
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=7
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 5 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-my-ways-are-higher-than-your-ways',
       E'My ways are higher than your ways — the unsearchable transcendence of Yahuah',
       E'The mercy that abundantly pardons the wicked (v.7) is grounded in a transcendence man cannot fathom: *For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith Yahuah (LORD). For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts* (Isaiah 55:8-9). The Father''s ways tower above man''s ways as the heavens above the earth. Paul breaks into the same doxology of wonder: *O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of Elohim (God)! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!* (Romans 11:33); *For who hath known the mind of the Lord? or who hath been his counsellor?* (Romans 11:34). None has known the mind of Yahuah; none has counselled him. The abundant pardon, the calling of the nations, the Word that does not return void — all flow from the higher ways that man cannot search out; his mercy is as far above human reckoning as the heavens are above the earth.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27362
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=8
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=9
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 6 (★★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-my-word-shall-not-return-unto-me-void',
       E'My word shall not return unto me void — the efficacious Word, the Formed Son sent forth',
       E'At the chapter''s heart is the efficacious Word: *For as the rain cometh down, and the snow from heaven, and returneth not thither, but watereth the earth, and maketh it bring forth and bud, that it may give seed to the sower, and bread to the eater: So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it* (Isaiah 55:10-11). The Word that goes forth out of Yahuah''s mouth and accomplishes is the Formed Son, the expressed Word drawn from the Formless: *In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with Elohim (God), and the Word was Elohim (God)... All things were made by him* (John 1:1,3); *And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us... full of grace and truth* (John 1:14). It is living and powerful: *the word of Elohim (God) is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword* (Hebrews 4:12). It abides forever: *Being born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, by the word of Elohim (God), which liveth and abideth for ever* (1 Peter 1:23); *the word of Yahuah (Lord) endureth for ever* (1 Peter 1:25). And the seed-and-harvest figure — the rain that gives *seed to the sower* — is the sower''s parable: *The sower soweth the word* (Mark 4:14). The Word sent forth always accomplishes that which Yahuah pleases; the spoken Word, made flesh, never returns void.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27365
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=10
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=11
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 7 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-55-ye-shall-go-out-with-joy-instead-of-the-thorn',
       E'Ye shall go out with joy — the second Exodus, the thorn-curse reversed, an everlasting sign',
       E'The chapter closes with the joyful return and creation restored: *For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace: the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing, and all the trees of the field shall clap their hands. Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree: and it shall be to Yahuah (LORD) for a name, for an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off* (Isaiah 55:12-13). This is the second-Exodus regathering — *the ransomed of Yahuah (LORD) shall return, and come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads: they shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away* (Isaiah 35:10). And the thorn that gives way to the fir tree is the reversal of Eden''s curse: *Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee* (Genesis 3:18) — the cursed ground healed, the fir and myrtle in place of thorn and brier. Paul names the groaning of creation released: *the earnest expectation of the creature waiteth for the manifestation of the sons of Elohim (God)* (Romans 8:19); *the creature itself also shall be delivered from the bondage of corruption into the glorious liberty of the children of Elohim (God)* (Romans 8:21). The redeemed go out with joy, the mountains sing, the trees clap their hands, the thorn-curse is reversed — and it is to Yahuah for a name, an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 27368
  FROM _s303_isa55_lookup sv, _s303_isa55_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=55 AND sv.verse_number=12
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=55 AND ev.verse_number=13
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

